From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] sapi: wave output device event source and sink, stream members, status, buffers, volume

sapi: wave output device event source and sink, stream members, status, buffers, volume

SpMMAudioOut's FIXME stubs, all returning E_NOTIMPL:

- ISpEventSource and ISpEventSink share the event queue of the voice
  (events.c): the notification kinds, SetInterest, GetEvents, GetInfo,
  AddEvents (what is not of interest is dropped, parameters are copied
  for the queue) and GetEventInterest. A new device is interested in
  nothing until it is told.
- IStream members of an output device: Read, CopyTo are STG_E_ACCESSDENIED,
  Seek only reports the position ((0, STREAM_SEEK_CUR) is the number of
  bytes written), SetSize, LockRegion, UnlockRegion and Clone are
  STG_E_INVALIDFUNCTION, Commit and Revert succeed (the data is already with
  the device), Stat describes a write-only stream whose size is what was
  written.
- SetState: STOP (drops what has not been played, the device stays open),
  PAUSE (waveOutPause, also opens a closed device paused) and RUN from
  PAUSE (waveOutRestart); other values are E_INVALIDARG.
- GetStatus (free buffer space from the buffer info and the bytes still
  queued, the bytes written, the state, the position the device has
  reached), Set/GetBufferInfo (50 ms notification, 500 ms buffer by
  default, zero sizes are E_INVALIDARG), Set/GetBufferNotifySize,
  GetDefaultFormat (22 kHz 16 bit mono), Get/SetVolumeLevel (0 to 10000
  through waveOutSetVolume, E_INVALIDARG above), GetMMHandle (the handle of
  the open device, SPERR_INVALID_AUDIO_STATE when closed).
- ISpObjectWithToken::SetObjectToken takes the device number from the
  token's DeviceId string value, when it is a number of an existing device.

